-# M4 fixture · legacy peer lower bound
-
-A dsh plugin declaring `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent: ^0.1.0-rc.8` in peer and dev
-dependencies. Under npm semver's prerelease rule this range does **not** match
-`0.1.2-alpha.2`, so installing into an alpha.2 profile emits "Issues with peer
-dependencies" warnings regardless of actual host compatibility (rollup R-08 #3).
-The README claim "the range guarantees host compatibility" is wrong. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+# M4 fixture · host-compatibility peer lower bound
+
+A dsh plugin whose documented host-compatibility entry point is the
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent` range in **peer and dev dependencies**. It ships the two
+surfaces such a plugin needs: the module entry point (`index.js`, a Cordis
+plugin exporting `inject` and `apply(ctx)`) and the bundle patch layer
+(`cordis.patch.yml`, declared as `dsh.bundle.patch` and inserted by a profile's
+`dsh.profile.bundles` list).
+
+The peer floor is the plugin's compatibility declaration, so it must name the
+host cohort the plugin was verified against. npm semver only lets a prerelease
+satisfy a range whose comparator carries the **same `major.minor.patch` tuple**
+and its own prerelease; a legacy floor such as `^0.1.0-rc.8` therefore does
+**not** match `0.1.2-alpha.2`. Installing into an alpha.2 profile emitted
+"Issues with peer dependencies" warnings regardless of actual host compatibility
+(rollup R-08 #3). The floor now names `^0.1.2-alpha.2` and must be rewritten on
+every cohort bump.
+
+The peer block also pins the plugin-protocol host, `@deepseek-ai/cordis: ^4.0.1`
+(peer and dev), because `ctx.effect` is Cordis API and the harness treats Cordis
+as a peer dependency of every package it hosts (root `AGENTS.md`:
+"`@deepseek-ai/cordis` is a peerDependency (+ dev) of every harness package").
+The cohort caret is `^4.0.1`; the alpha.2 tree's `cordis@4.0.2` satisfies it.
+Both floors are rewritten together on every cohort bump.
+
+The range is an install-time declaration on this host: `@deepseek-ai/dsh-app-boot`
+at `0.1.2-alpha.2` reads `peerDependencies` only to project module-fallback
+links, and nothing on the load path validates a declared range. Host-side
+preflight over a declared range is therefore carried as a patch
+(`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/plugin-host-compatibility-preflight/`); the patch
+retires once the harness owns that check. **Test material only — do not execute
+or publish** (`"private": true`).
